wifi: brcmfmac: report the signal of received action frames

The firmware reports the RSSI of every action frame it passes up in
struct brcmf_rx_mgmt_data, but brcmf_p2p_notify_action_frame_rx() hands
the frame to cfg80211 with a signal of 0, so NL80211_CMD_FRAME events
for action frames never carry NL80211_ATTR_RX_SIGNAL_DBM.

Pass the firmware's value instead. On a CYW43455 (firmware 7.45.265,
Raspberry Pi 3B+) it is the received signal in dBm, big-endian like the
other fields of the structure: a station registered for vendor-specific
Public Action frames now gets NL80211_ATTR_RX_SIGNAL_DBM with every
frame (92 of 100 frames from a peer about a metre away received, -24 to
-14 dBm, median -18 dBm; an ESP32-C6 next to them reported the same
transmitter at -22 dBm).

Tool use: this change was prepared with the help of an AI coding
assistant (Claude), which read the driver, wrote the change and the
changelog, and ran the test described in the cover letter; the
submitter reviewed and tested it.

(Upstream series for wireless-next, carried in Splanc's Pi images: pi/provisioning/nix/brcmfmac-actframe.nix.)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c
index 813cc15d8..f8e6cb4fa 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/p2p.c
@@ -1504,7 +1504,8 @@ int brcmf_p2p_notify_action_frame_rx(struct brcmf_if *ifp,
 					      NL80211_BAND_5GHZ);
 
 	wdev = &ifp->vif->wdev;
-	cfg80211_rx_mgmt(wdev, freq, 0, (u8 *)mgmt_frame, mgmt_frame_len, 0);
+	cfg80211_rx_mgmt(wdev, freq, (s32)be32_to_cpu(rxframe->rssi),
+			 (u8 *)mgmt_frame, mgmt_frame_len, 0);
 
 	kfree(mgmt_frame);
 	return 0;
